[38;2;169;177;214m  Upon connecting an OTG device when the application is not[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mrunning, the operating system broadcasts a specific USB[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mdevice attached action. This action triggers a system[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mdialog offering to launch a file manager. Selecting "OK" i[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mthis dialog then leads to the file list activity being[m
  [38;2;169;177;214minitiated with a corresponding intent action.[m
[38;2;169;177;214m  [m
[38;2;169;177;214m  [m
[38;2;169;177;214m  The `FileListActivity` should intercept the USB device[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mattach intent to launch `AddNtfsUsbActivity` instead of[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mopening the default file list. If `FileListActivity` is[m
  [38;2;169;177;214malready running, either `onNewIntent` or a broadcast[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mreceiver should handle the `ACTION_USB_DEVICE_ATTACHED`[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mevent. The single USB device should be automatically[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mselected in `AddNtfsUsbFragment`, triggering a permission[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mcheck and request if necessary.[m
[38;2;169;177;214m  [m
[38;2;169;177;214m  [m
[38;2;169;177;214m  A `BroadcastReceiver` will be implemented within[m
  [38;2;169;177;214m`AddNtfsUsbActivity` to handle both device attachment and[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mdetachment events. The activity will leverage an optional[m
  [38;2;169;177;214m`UsbDevice` passed via intent. Upon permission granted[m
  [38;2;169;177;214m(either through system dialog or `USB_DEVICE_ATTACHED`),[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mthe volume opens automatically, loading the root folder.[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mDevice detachment closes the volume and refreshes the[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mdevice list.[m
[38;2;169;177;214m  [m
[38;2;169;177;214m  [m
[38;2;169;177;214m  The `FileListActivity` needs to handle the[m
  [38;2;169;177;214m`ACTION_USB_DEVICE_ATTACHED` action within its `onCreate`[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mand `onNewIntent` methods. Upon receiving this intent, the[m
  [38;2;169;177;214m`UsbDevice` must be extracted and, if a USB Mass Storage[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mdevice, used to launch `AddNtfsUsbActivity`. A dynamic[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mreceiver or foreground check is required to handle device[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mattachments while the application is running, prompting th[m
  [38;2;169;177;214muser to open the device. Adding the `USB_DEVICE_ATTACHED`[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mintent filter to `AddNtfsUsbActivity` (or potentially both[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mactivities) will allow the system to offer the application[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mas an option when a USB drive is connected. This warrants[m
  [38;2;169;177;214mimmediate verification within the manifest to avoid[m
  [38;2;169;177;214munintended behavior.[m

